From 6aad2136954c2c9c107f3e68f53f0b440557dc46 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 17:34:40 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 21/21] wallpaper(ocs): scan per-image sidecars in the shared
 imported-ocs pack

Every OCS import lands in one persistent user-side collection
(Id=imported-ocs, Dir=~/.local/share/backgrounds/imported-ocs/) rather
than a fresh singleton pack per item. Per-image provenance lives in
<image-basename>.json sidecars next to each <image-basename>.jpg, so
discover() now scans sidecars instead of reading a per-pack pack.json,
and complete() validates each sidecar against the shared collection
identity.

WallpaperOcsImports.discover() rewrites the already imported check
to scan *.json sidecars in the collection directory and add one
provider:id per sidecar whose paired .jpg is also on disk. Old-shape
directories (one pack.json per import, left over from earlier testing)
contribute nothing and do not crash.

WallpaperOcsImports.complete() is rewritten for the new import payload:
- pack_id is now the fixed string imported-ocs, not a per-item id.
- pack_json is dropped; each entry under images carries the new
  sidecar basename instead.
- The shared collection must be registered (id=imported-ocs), the
  destination dir must exist, every per-image sidecar must exist on
  disk and parse to the active import key. The safety property the old
  class had -- never mark added unless real files actually landed
  under the right identity -- is preserved.

Tests in tests/wallpaper_ocs_test.vala are updated to the new payload
shape and add four cases: multi-sidecar discover in one shared dir,
orphan sidecar (no paired .jpg) being silently skipped, old-shape
directory being tolerated without crashing, and a payload missing the
new per-image sidecar field being rejected.
